{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/0h5cof","slideIndex":0,"text":"We built a small simulation to see whether error-mitigation tools can recover a useful measurement after noise is added. The assignment asks for SLC, NoiseLearnerV3, and PNA. This deck states clearly where the local simulator uses synthetic calibration rates in place of a hardware noise-learning job."}
