{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/2po36xcf","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":390,"top":253,"width":780,"height":46},"text":"SLC ranks errors by how much they can affect the chosen measurement.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#161616","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/3qx4f2dk","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":72,"top":322,"width":320,"height":36},"text":"3  Correct the result","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":25,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#8A3FFC","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/gnml4nu9","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":390,"top":322,"width":780,"height":46},"text":"PNA folds the modeled correction into the measured quantity.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#161616","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/1ov2dsvu","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":72,"top":422,"width":650,"height":40},"text":"Why not NoiseLearnerV3 here?","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#161616","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/x07e9sv2","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":72,"top":470,"width":1080,"height":90},"text":"Its official workflow submits learning jobs to IBM Quantum. No IBM account is configured on this computer, so local rates are simulated inputs, not hardware measurements.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#525252","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/0lxqcw","slideIndex":3,"text":"SLC assigns importance to candidate Pauli error terms and can trade a bounded bias for lower sampling cost. PNA propagates the inverse of learned noise into an observable. The official NoiseLearnerV3 accepts an IBM Quantum backend/service job; IBM documents that it has no local fake-backend mode. Sources: https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart.html ; https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-pna/tutorials/01_generate_noise_mitigating_observable.html ; https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives"}
