{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/toj2xgrq","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":72,"top":615,"width":1100,"height":30},"text":"At 1× noise, the SLC bias bound was 0.046 (under the 0.05 limit we set).","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#525252","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"chart","id":"ch/atgnitgj","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":70,"top":190,"width":700,"height":400},"name":"","chartType":"bar","title":"Error terms retained for PNA"}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/9vxbk4","slideIndex":4,"text":"At the middle noise setting, the learned model included 78 candidate error terms. SLC kept 53 for mitigation and set a bounded bias limit of 0.05. This reduced local PNA preprocessing from about 1.29 seconds to 1.13 seconds. The sampling-cost estimate fell from about 2.61 to 1.92."}
