{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/1wrqtoj6","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":75,"top":622,"width":1110,"height":48},"text":"PNA corrects a chosen measurement; it does not rebuild the full quantum state. These are simulator fidelity checks before measurement correction.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#525252","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"chart","id":"ch/mpczut4z","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":75,"top":185,"width":740,"height":410},"name":"","chartType":"line","title":"Exact simulated state fidelity before measurement correction"}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/cjcpw1","slideIndex":6,"text":"State fidelity is computed exactly from the noisy simulator density matrix against the ideal output. It drops from 0.833 at 0.5× noise to 0.488 at 2× noise. This metric is a separate check: PNA produces a corrected estimate for the selected observable, not a corrected full state."}
